"Sfx_IP9lsdQ": {
	"title": "One Fateful Knight - Shovel Knight",
	"wiki": "https://siivagunner.wiki/wiki/One%20Fateful%20Knight%20(Beta%20Mix)%20-%20Shovel%20Knight",
	"joke": [
		Text  Visual  Explanation   {"time": "0:08", "joke": "Shovel knight making his guest appearance in Shmegdul Bobbin's Vacuuming Adventure with 56 Steam reviews - A clip of the movie Elf, featuring Buddy the Elf walking down the streets of New York.'},
		Refers to Shovel Knight's prolific guest appearance rate in other video games."Shmegdul Bobbin's Vacuuming Adventure" is not a real game, and its mention is merely a setup for the joke at 2:40.   {"time": "0:11", "joke": "VVVVVV fans when there's a 0.2 cm tall rock in front of them - A clip from the movie Doctor Strange, in which the titular Dr. Strange is sent flying into other dimensions."},
		In VVVVVV, small bumps or steps require the player to entirely flip gravity to get over them, which is often a very convoluted process in comparison to jumping in most other platformers.   {"time": "0:14", "joke": "Celeste fans spending 2000 hours to beat level 9 z-side without slowing down, touching the ground or breathing - A GIF of a man licking his lips."},
		 In Celeste, there are optional strawberry collectables scattered across the game. When the player touches a strawberry, the player has to land on ground to instantly collect it, so never touching the ground while collecting every strawberry in the level is a particularly hard challenge mixed with the high difficulty of the game.   {"time": "0:16", "joke": "Meat Boy Fans waiting for the Hell boss to bash his skull into the ground for the third time and kill himself - A clip of Mr. Bean waiting from the movie Mr. Bean's Holiday."},
		As the slander implies, the Little Horn boss fight of Chapter 4: Hell in Super Meat Boy is defeated when the boss slams its head into the ground for the third time, particularly after multiple sets of attacks the player must dodge.   {"time": "0:19", "joke": "Rain World - A scene from Moana where Moana is almost eaten by a monster before a different monster eats it."},
		 References Rain World's enemies, particularly their hostility towards each other.   {"time": "0:21", "joke": "Cave Story fans fighting off a swarm of insects - A clip from "Superman IV - Nostalgia Critic", where the Nostalgia Critic is flailing around with a gun."},
		 Cave Story has several insectoid enemies: beetles, basu, and gaudis.   {"time": "0:24", "joke": "Fez fans when black monolith - Charlie Kelly explaining about Pepe Silvia from the It's Always Sunny In Philadelphia episode "Sweet Dee Has a Heart Attack"."},
		There is an optional black monolith puzzle to which the solution is known in FEZ, but the latter part of the solution was brute-forced by players. It is still currently unknown how the player was actually meant to come to the full solution (one solution purported to be the actual solution was discredited).   {"time": "0:27", "joke": "Terraria fans when they get into an argument - A clip from Terraria Trolls by Corridor."},
		 References Terraria's melee swing animation.   {"time": "0:30", "joke": "FTL fans ideal society - A cutscene from Aperture Desk Job where the praying mantises have created a functioning society."},
		 In Faster Than Light, players can use crew teleporters to send Mantis Boarders, a race with increased attack and speed, to board hostile ships, allowing them to kill the crew and take the ship for better rewards.   {"time": "0:32", "joke": "Dead Cells fans expert strategy for opening doors - This GIF of a man breaking through a door."},
		 In Dead Cells, breaking through doors is often much faster than opening them.   {"time": "0:35", "joke": "Spelunky fans when there's a bat outside their window - A clip from UHF of Raul Hernandez throwing a poodle out a window.'},
		References the usage of dogs as projectiles in the Spelunky franchise.   {"time": "0:37", "joke": "Eastward fans when they find out they can't use tofu and lemon to make pizza - A clip of Gordon Ramsay from Hell's Kitchen, shouting and slamming a table'},
		In Eastward, tofu is classified as "Dairy and Eggs" and lemon is classified as "Fruit", which can be used to make a pizza in-game.   {"time": "0:40", "joke": "Hotline Miami 2 - "Louisoix Levelilleur's Final Moments" GIF'},
		The ending of Hotline Miami 2: Wrong Number sees San Francisco getting nuked by Russia. The way the cutscenes depict the characters getting caught in the blast is similar to how Levelilleur dies, that being engulfed in light as it fades to white.   {"time": "0:43", "joke": "Binding of isaac fans when they see dog turds on the sidewalk - Gameplay footage from Conker's Bad Fur Day where Conker's eyes spin with dollar signs, normally seen when collecting Cash."},
		References the positive effects of breaking Poops in The Binding of Isaac, specifically the ability to collect Coins from them.   {"time": "0:46", "joke": "The Messenger stopping the game to dump all its lore before the final boss - A clip from Thanos Test Footage."},
		 In The Messenger, after the player collects all of the Music Notes and places them onto the wall in the Tower of Time HQ, a cutscene plays that tells the backstory of the game before entering Music Box, the final area of the game.   {"time": "0:48", "joke": "Hyper light drifter fans watching a story cutscene with no clue what's going on - "Staring Kanye" GIF."},
		References the cutscenes in Hyper Light Drifter, in which there is no readable dialogue.   {"time": "0:51", "joke": "Tower of Heaven fans when they touch grass (the book of laws states they much not touch any living thing) - Gameplay footage of Half-Life 2 in which a Combine soldier disintegrates, taken directly from this YouTube video."},
		 References the main gameplay mechanic (The Book of Laws and the added rules they provide) of Tower of Heaven, which include "no touching any living thing".   {"time": "0:54", "joke": "playing Castle Crashers - The "Cheap Fighting Combo" option from Completing the Mission where Henry beats up Right Hand Man Reborn using a prolonged uppercut-double divekick combo."},
		 The combo based beat-em-up system Castle Crashers uses is capable of juggling (keeping an enemy in the air via aerial attacks, thus making them unable to respond to attacks) enemies from hit to death, and is one of the key elements the game is known for.   {"time": "0:56", "joke": "Braid fans trying to unlock their front door (it's on the right side of their house) - Footage of Mickey Mouse struggling to open a door, taken from the 1937 cartoon Lonesome Ghosts."},
		The house that serves as the hub in Braid is structured so that the front door is on the left side of its map (the right from the perspective of the player character when inside the house).   {"time": "0:59", "joke": "Hollow Knight fans fighting Radiant Markoth - A scene from the Rick and Morty episode "The Ricklantis Mixup", where two Mortys play in a casino. One Morty in particular is playing a slot machine called "Story Train Slots""},
		 References Radiant Markoth's intense difficulty and randomness in moves.   {"time": "1:02", "joke": "Stardew Valley fans do not use the wiki to compulsively stalk everyone challenge - The "Thug Tug" scene from The SpongeBob SquarePants Movie where a thug tries to goad an increasingly nervous SpongeBob and Patrick to sing the "I'm a Goofy Goober" song."},
		References Stardew Valley players using the Stardew Valley Wiki extensively in order to optimize playing the game, notably to give gifts to and schedule meetups with the townsfolk.   {"time": "1:04", "joke": "Undertale and Deltarune fans fighting over which pale stumpy trash goblin is sexier - Footage of Reggie Fils-Amié and Satoru Iwata fighting, taken directly from the Mii Fighter reveal trailer for Super Smash Bros. for Nintendo 3DS and Wii U."},
		 References Sans from Undertale and Spamton from Deltarune, two secret bosses from each respective games who have gained notoriety in the fandoms for their backstories, fights, and the fans who are attracted to them. The latter earned Sans and Spamton the infamous "Tumblr Sexyman" status, despite the fact that both of them are short, stout, pale, and not conventionally attractive.   {"time": "1:07", "joke": "Necrodancer fans bangin to the zone boss theme for 8 seconds before it dies - A sped-up GIF of Jerma985 air-playing the drums"},
		 Crypt of the NecroDancer is a game that mixes elements of action RPGs and rhythm games. The only way to make the player do any action in-game is by performing to the beat of the accompanying song, which can limit how much the player hears of said song.   {"time": "1:10", "joke": "Factorio fans explaining the intricacies of their 30k spm gigabase to the wendys cashier - "Ibai Llanos Explaining Things" GIF"},
		 In Factorio, players can make complicated factory lines and logistic systems in an attempt to achieve peak science efficiency   {"time": "1:12", "joke": "World of Goo fans killing the third dimension with targeted ads - Footage from Apple's "1984" Macintosh commercial.'},
		Chapter 3 of World of Goo ends with the World of Goo Corporation transforming the world into 3D, rendering most of the 2D citizens incompatible. Chapter 4 of the game ends with the player flooding the World of Goo Corporation HQ with undeleted spam emails in order to overload its servers and shut its 3D product down.   {"time": "1:15", "joke": "Oneshot fans when someone calls them by their real name irl (fourth wall break) - A scene of Wee-Bey's incredulous reaction from The Wire episode "The Hunt"."},
		In OneShot, the game pulls the name of the player from the name of the active user on the computer running it rather than naming the player in-game, therefore causing a "fourth wall break".   {"time": "1:17", "joke": "Papers please fans in tsa after letting through the funny lil guy with the crayon passport - A scene from Johnny English where a building explodes behind English, which then he awkwardly glances at."},
		 In Papers Please, multiple times in the game, a smuggler by the name of Jorji Costava will attempt to enter Arstotzka with incorrect documents, which the player will usually reject. In one of these attempts, he attempts to enter with a fake passport that he drew himself.   {"time": "1:20", "joke": "Stanley Parable fans after pushing a button for 4 hours - An animated version of Consciousness by Nick Keller."},
		 References the Art Ending of The Stanley Parable (and The Stanley Parable: Ultra Deluxe), achieved after 4 hours of repeat gameplay of pushing buttons.   {"time": "1:23", "joke": "Cuphead fans go 5 seconds without smoke bomb equipped challenge - "Sweaty Speedrunner" GIF."},
		 In Cuphead: Don't Deal with the Devil (and the Delicious Last Course DLC), the Smoke Bomb charm allows the player to dash through normally damaging stage elements, and generally as seen as one of, if not the best charm in the game by fans.   {"time": "1:26", "joke": "Baba is You fans thinking they've finally finished the game for the 5th time, immidiately greeted by 35 new aneurism-difficulty levels in the colon themed world - A Team Fortress 2 recreation of a GIF of a man eagerly opening a fridge then turning away disappointed.'},
		Refers to the fake endings that can be found when playing Baba Is You.   {"time": "1:28", "joke": "Among Us fans when the Blues scale plays - A sped-up version of the "Gemini31292's Seizure Reaction" GIF."},
		The Blues scale includes the sequential notes of "Dead Body Reported" from Among Us.   {"time": "1:31", "joke": "Hat in Time world 3 - A scene from The Princess and the Frog where Dr. Facilier makes a deal with Prince Naveen."},
		 References the story of Subcon Forest, the third chapter of A Hat in Time. A prominent character in the chapter is The Snatcher, who forces Hat Kid to sign a deal with him for her soul.   {"time": "1:34", "joke": "Bastion fans with dueling pistols equipped - An edited version of the "Fat Man Shoots Pistol" video with the footage mirrored and the man's shirt colored red."},
		References how the player shoots when having two pistols equipped in Bastion.   {"time": "1:36", "joke": "playing yume nikki - "The Weeknd Looking Around" GIF."},
		 References how Yume Nikki's gameplay is mainly based on wandering around various worlds, which are often labyrinthine and easy to get lost in, and finding interesting things over more traditional gameplay objectives.   {"time": "1:39", "joke": "Hiveswap fans betting on which terrible business decision What Pumpkin will make next - A scene from the Jack Ryan episode "Black 22" where Victor Polizzi pushes his chips in."},
		 References Hiveswap's troubled development, as well as What Pumpkin, the company responsible for publishing and managing Hiveswap and the larger Homestuck franchise.   {"time": "1:42", "joke": "I think Matpat will enjoy dissecting this frame by frame - A clip of "The Brick Wall "Talks Politics"" by Marionzo Vance."},
		 References a series of tweets from tinyBuild, the publisher of the Hello Neighbor franchise, which attempted (and failed) to convince MatPat to analyze Hello Neighbor: The Animated Series as part of his Game Theory series.   {"time": "1:44", "joke": "Omori fans when ayo the pizza here - An edited clip of the Breaking Bad episode "Hermanos" where Gus Fring stands silently in an elevator."},
		 Refers to the "Ayo the pizza here" Vine by CalebCity, which in turn is often associated with a major plot point of OMORI.   {"time": "1:47", "joke": "The Escapist fans getting themselves arrested so they can play their favourite game in real life - A clip of Bobby Brown from The Bobby Brown Story getting arrested while smiling."},
		 References the setting of The Escapist, prison.   {"time": "1:50", "joke": "Night in the Woods fans 92% of the way into the chill slice of life coming of age story - A clip of the Zombie Land Saga episode "Good Morning SAGA" where Minamoto Sakura gets hit by a truck."},
		 References the sudden horror-esque events that happen very far into Night in the Woods' story.   {"time": "1:52", "joke": "Vampire Survivors fans when they go shopping on black friday - A clip from the video "Extreme Whipcracker: Adam Winrich" by Volume One"},
		 References the main gameplay loop of Vampire Survivors (slaughtering crowds of enemies with weapons).   {"time": "1:55", "joke": "Outer Wilds fans when you spoil that there's a spaceship in the game without a two paragraph content warning and a password authenticated spoiler tag - A clip of the "honey trial" scene from Bee Movie where Layton reacts hysterically after getting stung by Adam."},
		References how the Outer Wilds' community dislikes people revealing spoilers since it's a knowledge-based game meant to be played blind.   {"time": "1:58", "joke": "Disco Elysium fans in their basement writing Animal Farm fanfiction - The "Gunna Writing Fire" GIF."},
		 References how the differing political ideologies of people and nations play important roles in Disco Elysium's plot and setting, with the slander poking fun at how such a politically-charged game might seem to be an unusual match for a conventional fandom (Animal Farm being a political satire by George Orwell).   {"time": "2:00", "joke": "Slay the Spire fans crafting their perfect Blasphemy + Vault synergy - A clip of from the music video for "Get Your Shine On" by Birdman ft. Lil Wayne of Birdman rubbing his hands together while looking out a window."},
		 Using the Blasphemy + Vault synergy combo in Slay the Spire instantly kills the player.   {"time": "2:03", "joke": "Henry Stickmin fans when they don't get to retry from the last decision after dying a horrifying and painful death - A GIF of a sped up skeleton burning with flames surrounding it."},
		References the Replay mechanic in the Henry Stickmin franchise, in which players are allowed to reload save files to choose alternative story choices.   {"time": "2:06", "joke": "Lisa fans when they hear someone having an aneurysm on the keyboard - A clip from the Sesame Street song "Change the Plan"."},
		 References the unusual instrumentation and samples used in LISA: The Painful songs such as "All Hail the Fishmen" and "Work Harder".   {"time": "2:09", "joke": "Average yiik fan - A GIF of a custom "Chad Thundercock"-themed fighter striding from Soulcalibur VI."},
		 References the ironic popularity of YIIK: A Post-Modern RPG.   {"time": "2:11", "joke": "BitTripRunner fans 2023 meetup - A clip of The Fresh Prince of Bel Air episode "I, Done" where Will ponders over the Banks family's empty living room."},
		The slander pokes fun of the niche popularity of BIT.TRIP RUNNER, implying that the game isn't popular enough to warrant a sizeable fanbase.   {"time": "2:14", "joke": "Va-11 hall-a fans concocting the most revolting beverage imaginable - A scene from the Breaking Bad episode "Sunset", where Walter White is seen manufacturing drugs."},
		 Refers to the main gameplay mechanic of creating drinks based on clients' preferences to reveal story elements in VA-11 Hall-A: Cyberpunk Bartender Action. The caption itself references the "Weebs making the worst memes in existence" meme using the aforementioned Breaking Bad scene.   {"time": "2:17", "joke": "Your Turn To Die fans when Joe Mama - A clip from the SpongeBob SquarePants episode "Fools in April" where Squidward laughs hysterically when pranking SpongeBob."},
		 References the character Joe Tazuna from Your Turn to Die -Death Game By Majority- and how often he is used to reference the "Joe Mama" meme.   {"time": "2:19", "joke": "Bendy and the Ink Machine fans in the mall when they see a cardboard cutout - This GIF of a store employee grabbing an axe."},
		 References the usage of Bendy cardboard cutouts as setpieces/jumpscares in both Bendy and the Ink Machine and Bendy and the Dark Revival.   {"time": "2:22", "joke": "Slender fans in the same mall eyeing the mannequins in the menswear section - This GIF of a girl doing the "I'm watching you!" gesture.'},
		References the faceless depiction of the Slenderman and how he looks like a mannequin.   {"time": "2:25", "joke": "Garten of Banban players after finishing the game realizing they've had the best video game experience of all time - A clip of Thanos smiling from Avengers: Infinity War."},
		References the mass ironic fandom of the Garten of Banban series.   {"time": "2:27", "joke": "FNF fans in 2054 still waiting for the game to come out - A clip from Saving Private Ryan where a young Ryan crossfades into his elderly self."},
		 References the extended development time of Friday Night Funkin' (the first release of the demo in 2020 to the current development of the full title as of 2023).   {"time": "2:30", "joke": "Geometry Dash fans rushing to flood the comment section on the latest obscure Newgrounds song used in the new hardest demon level - A GIF of a large crowd of people rushing into a store."},
		 Custom Geometry Dash levels uploaded by players allow the usage of audio uploaded to Newgrounds instead of/alongside official levels' song. As a result, when a level gets popular, players will often visit and comment on the audio said level used.   {"time": "2:32", "joke": "Eversion - A GIF sequence of the "Mr. Incredible Becoming Uncanny" meme."},
		 References the main mechanic of Eversion, which involves changing the current stage's state to a slightly different version of the stage, and this ability can be used recursively. Progressing through a level may require the player to go through multiple versions of the same level, each of which become more progressively gruesome and disturbing the deeper the player goes.   {"time": "2:35", "joke": "Iconoclasts fans when they see a pool of milk - This GIF of a woman jumping down the side of a cliff in heels."},
